  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Lofted pass over the board",
  "description": "Place two cones a little outside the penalty area, one on each side. Lay a loose piece of board (or another low obstacle) between them – the two cones in the middle show where it lies. Group A stands behind the left cone with balls, group B behind the right cone.\n\nA skates round their cone with the ball and plays a lofted pass over the board to B, who has rounded the other cone at the same time and is heading for goal. B brings the ball down and finishes. Rotation: A goes to B and B to A.\n\nThe board forces a real lofted ball. Variant: finish first time, or add a defender who starts at the goal. Switch sides so everyone lofts in both directions. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Timing: B should come into the rink at speed just as the ball is lofted."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Get the blade under the ball – it must clear the board and land in front of B."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "B brings the ball down softly with the stick or skate and looks at the goal straight away."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Finish quickly – shot, drag or deflection depending on the situation."
    }
  ],
